rror_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 21110, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PB3qihsgEUwxDe6WcA2XAH", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 21110, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017JQvLBouQU2iK5zQgsTdHX", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 21410, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017JQvLBouQU2iK5zQgsTdHX", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 21410, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017JQvLBouQU2iK5zQgsTdHX", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25768, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01NBTw7r2v42a1K1MVvDUo5d", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. (The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging.) I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions. A retry finished the rollout to all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, service healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and of the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56368, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01NBTw7r2v42a1K1MVvDUo5d", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56368, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01NBTw7r2v42a1K1MVvDUo5d", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 61517, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01JWdySSTRPc3v3HD8cMMt5M", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. (The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging.) I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions. A retry finished the rollout to all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, service healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and of the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 62117, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JWdySSTRPc3v3HD8cMMt5M", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 62117, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JWdySSTRPc3v3HD8cMMt5M", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63779, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01AtSp93jsU1TSNRDbY7iVbL", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 64079, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01AtSp93jsU1TSNRDbY7iVbL", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 64079, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01AtSp93jsU1TSNRDbY7iVbL", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 69414, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in every region, and the service is healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident for it.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. My first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I ran the same rollback again and it finished. All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate has dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 and has paged on-call. It describes the failed v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, the current state, and follow-up items. My first request timed out. I sent it again with the same idempotency key so it couldn't create a second incident, and I confirmed only one exists.\n\nTwo things still need looking into: why v2.3.1 failed (its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy in staging) and what caused the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0157KVsVvYmLhuS787EBjRuV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018dUp42W2PPZANSjF95WL8r", "caller": 