, with an error rate of about 18%. (The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging.) I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions. A retry finished the rollout to all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, service healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and of the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so I can't tell if the incident was created. Retrying with the same idempotency key is safe and won't open a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JWdySSTRPc3v3HD8cMMt5M", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. (The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging.) I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions. A retry finished the rollout to all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, service healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and of the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01AtSp93jsU1TSNRDbY7iVbL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in every region, and the service is healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident for it.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. My first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I ran the same rollback again and it finished. All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate has dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 and has paged on-call. It describes the failed v2.3.1 deploy, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, the current state, and follow-up items. My first request timed out. I sent it again with the same idempotency key so it couldn't create a second incident, and I confirmed only one exists.\n\nTwo things still need looking into: why v2.3.1 failed (its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy in staging) and what caused the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}